Task 
Your task is to disable direct SSH root login on all app servers(3) within the Stratos Datacenter.

Context
By default you are on a jump host, you are to ssh into the 3 App servers and disable direct SSH root login respectively
using their UserName, ServerName and Password as given

Solution
For App Server 1(stapp01)
ssh tony@stapp01
sudo vi /etc/ssh/sshd_config  <this commmand gets you into a text editor to edit the file>
type ‘i’ to get on insert mode.
<Find the line containing PermitRootLogin. It might be commented out with a # and set to yes, or explicitly set to yes.
If it's commented out (#PermitRootLogin yes), uncomment it and change yes to no.
If it's uncommented (PermitRootLogin yes), change yes to no.>
Save by typing :x  <this saves as well as exits the text editor>
sudo systemctl restart sshd
systemctl status sshd <this will show the sshd service is running>
exit

